  "authTierOverall": "T1_SIMPLE",
  "authTierRationale": "The connector offers two credential modes and the easiest is 'Access Token': a single self-serve secret (a Shopify Admin API access token obtained by creating a custom app in the store admin) sent as the X-Shopify-Access-Token header. No app registration, no client id/secret, no refresh token, no token exchange in the connector. The alternative 'Shopify OAuth' mode requires the user to register their own Shopify app and supply client_id + client_secret, which is T2_BYO_APP standalone; Estuary's hosted control plane fills those in via the declared oauth2 authUrlTemplate/accessTokenUrlTemplate (x-oauth2-provider: shopify), so hosted users do no work, but the standalone tier is T2. Note that even the OAuth mode's config requires access_token as a required property, and no refresh_token field exists anywhere in the schema (Shopify offline access tokens do not expire), so it is not T3.",

  "unionMisfits": [
    {
      "where": "streams[*].pull.*.paginator",
      "description": "The paginator is a hybrid the union does not name. The token is read from the HTTP `Link` response header (rel=\"next\") as a FULL URL, but that URL is NOT followed verbatim: only its query string is parsed out and re-applied as the query params of a request whose scheme/host/path are rebuilt from url_base + stream path. So it is neither `next_url` (not verbatim) nor a `cursor` with a single named cursorParam (the code forwards ALL query params opaquely; it never names page_info or limit). Classified here as cursor + tokenFrom:header + tokenTo:query_param with cursorParam null. A second wrinkle: pagination also stops when the response body is falsy, not only when the Link header lacks rel=\"next\", so terminateOn is really absent_token OR empty_body.",
      "proposedShape": {
        "type": "cursor",
        "tokenFrom": "header_link_url",
        "tokenTo": "query_param_set",
        "tokenIsOpaqueQueryString": true,
        "carriesAllQueryParams": true,
        "rebuildsPathFromStreamDefinition": true,
        "terminateOn": ["absent_token", "empty_body"]
      }
    },
    {
      "where": "credentialModes[1].tier",
      "description": "The 'Shopify OAuth' mode requires client_id AND client_secret AND access_token as required config properties, but there is no refresh_token. The T1/T2/T3 ladder has no rung for 'bring your own app plus a non-expiring access token'. Scored T2_BYO_APP because app registration is the dominant cost and no refresh token is asked for, but a standalone user must actually complete the OAuth dance themselves to obtain the access_token, which is strictly more work than T2 implies.",
      "proposedShape": { "tier": "T2_BYO_APP", "extraUserSuppliedTokens": ["access_token"], "refreshTokenRequired": false, "hostedControlPlaneFillsClientCredentials": true }
    },
    {
      "where": "streams[*].pull.backfill vs .incremental",
      "description": "There is no distinct backfill request shape. Backfill and incremental are the SAME path, records path and paginator; they differ only in which timestamp query param the shared get_url_params emits: created_at_min=<start_date> when no state exists, updated_at_min=<checkpointed value> once it does. The orders stream overrides this and uses updated_at_min in both cases (plus status=any and order=updated_at asc). Splitting into two PullSpecs duplicates almost everything.",
